GNU Wget is a free software package for retrieving files using HTTP, HTTPS and FTP,
the most widely-used Internet protocols. It is a non-interactive commandline tool,
so it may easily be called from scripts, cron jobs, terminals without X-Windows support, etc.

This port is based on GNU Wget 1.20.3, compiled with HTTPS support via the AROS
port of OpenSSL 1.1.0h.

The build follows the AROS contrib port conventions: the sources are fetched,
patched with wget-1.20.3-aros.diff and built with %fetch_and_build_gnu_development
(see mmakefile.src). The binary is installed both under Development/bin and in
Extras:Networking/Apps/Wget.

When you start wget the first time it will complain that it misses the file env:wgetcfg.
You can either create an empty file (echo "" >env:wgetcfg) or better copy the file
sample.wgetrc (copy sample.wgetrc env:wgetcfg and copy sample.wgetrc envarc:wgetcfg).
The build already installs a default sample into ENVARC:wgetcfg.

Notes on the AROS port:
- Background mode (-b) and --use-askpass are not supported (AROS has no fork()).
- IPv6 is disabled (AROS network stacks are IPv4 based).
- The OpenSSL version shipped with AROS is 1.1.0h, so TLS 1.3 is not available.
- --timeout/--connect-timeout/--read-timeout for connect, DNS and SSL reads are
  not enforced by a signal/alarm (AROS has no alarm()/setitimer()); the
  underlying network stack's own timeouts apply instead.

Type wget --help for a short help. The file wget.info contains documentation.